1. **A method for producing an organopolysiloxane emulsion composition having a reduced octamethylcyclotetrasiloxane content**, the method comprising:

   (a) preparing a mixture comprising  
   (i) an organosiloxane starting material comprising at least one cyclic siloxane, linear siloxane, or mixture thereof,  
   (ii) at least one surfactant, and  
   (iii) water;

   (b) emulsifying the mixture to form an aqueous siloxane emulsion in which siloxane droplets have an average particle size of **not more than 500 nm**;

   (c) adding an acid catalyst to the aqueous siloxane emulsion, or using an acid surfactant as at least part of the surfactant, thereby providing acidic conditions suitable for emulsion polymerization;

   (d) subjecting the aqueous siloxane emulsion to acid-catalyzed emulsion polymerization to form an organopolysiloxane dispersed in water, wherein the organopolysiloxane has a viscosity of **at least 10,000 mPa·s at 25°C**;

   (e) optionally neutralizing the emulsion after polymerization; and

   (f) recovering an organopolysiloxane emulsion composition,

   wherein the recovered organopolysiloxane emulsion composition has an average particle size of **not more than 1,000 nm** and contains octamethylcyclotetrasiloxane in an amount of **not more than 1,000 ppm by mass**, based on the mass of the organopolysiloxane contained in the emulsion composition.
